sections.content:
Panel members may be engaged to deliver a range of pest animal management activities, including but not limited to:
- Planning and implementation of pest animal control programs;
- Ground and aerial baiting programs (where appropriately licensed and authorised);
- Trapping, shooting and other approved control methods;
- Monitoring, surveillance and assessment of pest animal populations and impacts;
- Data collection, record keeping and reporting on works undertaken; Landholder liaison and stakeholder engagement;
- Compliance with relevant legislation, permits, biosecurity requirements and industry best practice standards;
- Supply of labour, equipment, materials and consumables necessary to undertake the services.
Services may be required across a variety of landscapes, including agricultural land, conservation areas, public land and other locations within the North Coast Local Land Services region. Contractors must be capable of operating safely in remote and challenging environments and demonstrate appropriate qualifications, licences, insurances and work health and safety systems.
The panel will be used to procure pest animal management services for projects of varying scale and complexity over the term of the arrangement. Inclusion on the panel does not guarantee any work. NCLLS will engage panel members based on project requirements, contractor capability, location, availability and value for money considerations.
